\paragraph{Routing robustness across depth.}
The gradient extends to classification robustness: VLA-trained achieves $100\%$ at L1 through L31; untrained achieves $100\%$ at L1 but decays to $82\%$ by L31 (fragile incidental routing).
Llama-2 base shows an intermediate pattern: L1 accuracy is $80.2\%$, rising to $100\%$ by L5, suggesting that pretrained representations encode general language structure rather than instruction identity per se.

