\subsubsection{L1 Attention Pattern Analysis}
\label{sec:attention_pattern}

See Figure~\ref{fig:attention} and Table~\ref{tab:routing_gradient} (main text) for the per-head attention distribution at L1 across three conditions.
The three-level gradient (untrained 0/32, Llama-2 base 9/32, VLA-trained 25/32 instruction-dominant heads) shows that language pretraining seeds partial instruction routing and VLA fine-tuning amplifies it.
Llama-2 base achieves $80.2\%$ cross-instruction accuracy at L1 (vs.\ $100\%$ for both untrained and VLA-trained), rising to $100\%$ by L5, consistent with pretrained representations encoding general language structure rather than instruction identity.

